From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:07:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: keep a linear image linear, minus input usage

get_image_usage_for_feats() gives a render target INPUT_ATTACHMENT
usage unless it is both LINEAR and SHARED (and a stream output target
always), and a render target or a depth/stencil target FEEDBACK_LOOP
usage where the extension is there, in case gallium needs them. V3DV
takes no input attachment on a linear image, which it cannot sample
(the same check in 24.0.7 and 26.x), so the check of
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR fails (VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, usage
0x93) and zink makes the image with optimal tiling. A linear dma-buf
then holds a tiled image: in DomU on a Raspberry Pi 5 host,
agl-compositor on zink scanned out garbage, and a 356x400 linear
client buffer was sized as a 384-wide tiled image, measured on
2026-10-17 with clients made linear for the display planes.

Where get_image_usage() falls back to DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR and the
check fails with either bit set, try again without them, and return
the usage without the bits that were dropped. The other tilings and
the HOST_TRANSFER retry are unchanged. Such an image has no input
attachment or feedback loop usage, so framebuffer fetch on it, or a
feedback loop layout, is not valid. Nor, on V3DV, has it SAMPLED
usage: an imported linear client buffer, which used to get a tiled
image (that failed to import or held the wrong layout), now gets a
linear one that cannot be sampled, so a compositor that composes it
with the GPU instead of a plane issues an invalid sampling, which
reaches the host's GPU under Venus.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -67,6 +67,12 @@
 #define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR 0
 #endif
 
+/* usage zink adds to a render target in case gallium needs it, and may
+ * drop for a linear dma-buf image (see double_check_ici)
+ */
+#define ZINK_LINEAR_OPTIONAL_USAGE (VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT | \
+                                    VK_IMAGE_USAGE_ATTACHMENT_FEEDBACK_LOOP_BIT_EXT)
+
 #if defined(__APPLE__)
 // Source of MVK_VERSION
 #include "MoltenVK/vk_mvk_moltenvk.h"
@@ -537,6 +543,17 @@
       ici->pNext = fmt_list;
       ici->flags |= VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT;
    }
+#if defined(ZINK_USE_DMABUF) && !defined(_WIN32)
+   /* A DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR image may be refused only for the usage zink
+    * adds in case gallium ever needs it: V3DV takes no input attachment on
+    * a linear image, which it cannot sample. Falling back to another tiling
+    * would break the linear dma-buf the image is for (a scanout or an
+    * import), so try again without that usage; the caller sees what was
+    * dropped in ici->usage.
+    */
+   if (*mod == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR && (usage & ZINK_LINEAR_OPTIONAL_USAGE))
+      return double_check_ici(screen, ici, usage & ~ZINK_LINEAR_OPTIONAL_USAGE, mod);
+#endif
    return false;
 }
 
@@ -585,8 +602,9 @@
          if (feats) {
             VkImageUsageFlags usage = get_image_usage_for_feats(screen, feats, templ, bind, &need_extended);
             assert(!need_extended);
+            /* without the optional usage double_check_ici() may have dropped */
             if (double_check_ici(screen, ici, usage, mod))
-               return usage;
+               return usage & (ici->usage | ~ZINK_LINEAR_OPTIONAL_USAGE);
          }
       }
    } else {
